  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-usage-limits",
      "text": "A DeepSeek Harness (DSH) plugin that shows how much of your Claude and Codex plan limits you have used:\nan omp-style line in the terminal client (`dst`, dsh-TUI) and a ring meter in dsh web. The product and\ntechnical specification is [SPEC.md](SPEC.md); the test plan and evidence are in [TESTING.md](TESTING.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it shows",
      "text": "**dst.** One coloured line above the prompt, on the first screen (Launchpad) and in chat, in the format of\nJake's omp line:\n\n```\nClaude (proxy) 5h ░░░░░░░░ 1% ↻2h29m 7d ██░░░░░░ 29% ↻5d6h   Codex (proxy) 7d █░░░░░░░ 12% ↻3d11h\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "What it shows",
      "text": "Each account shows its 5-hour and weekly windows: a bar, the percent used and the time to the reset.\nPercents are green below 50%, amber from 50% and red from 80%. A narrow terminal drops the bars, then\nthe reset times, then shortens names (`Claude·px`), and finally shows only the fullest window. A refresh\nthat fails keeps the last numbers and marks the account `stale`. Nothing shows until data arrives."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it shows",
      "text": "**dsh web.** A small ring and label beside the composer's context meter in a session, for example\n`Codex (proxy) 7d 52%`: the fullest 5-hour or weekly window, coloured by the same thresholds. Click it for a\npanel that lists every window of every account, including per-model windows such as `Weekly · Fable`\nand extra Codex limits, with reset times and stale or error notes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Where the data comes from",
      "text": "Accounts, in display order:\n\n| Account | Source |\n|---|---|\n| `Claude (proxy)`, `Codex (proxy)` | [ProviderProxy](https://github.com/jakehemmerle/providerproxy): `GET <baseURL>/usage/claude` and `/usage/chatgpt` with the proxy client key from `PROVIDERPROXY_API_KEY` (or `proxy.apiKeyEnv`) |\n| `Claude`, `Codex` | DSH's own sign-ins (`llm-pi-ai/anthropic`, `llm-pi-ai/openai-codex`) → `https://api.anthropic.com/api/oauth/usage`, `https://chatgpt.com/backend-api/wham/usage` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Where the data comes from",
      "text": "An account that is not configured is left out. The plugin never refreshes, writes or logs tokens; an\nexpired sign-in waits for DSH to refresh it. ProviderProxy accounts are read at most once a minute (the\nproxy caches its upstream for a minute); direct sign-ins at most every `minIntervalMs` (default 5 minutes,\nnever below 1 minute), with back-off after errors. `dst` asks every minute and redraws reset times every\n30 seconds without a request; the web page polls the plugin's route every minute."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Both rows are generated by nix-config (`home/dsh.nix`); by hand they are:\n\n```yaml"
    },
    {
      "section": "~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "- insert:\n    - id: usage-limits\n      name: /path/to/dsh-usage-limits/index.js\n      config: &usage\n        minIntervalMs: 300000\n        proxy:\n          baseURL: http://gpu.tail47033e.ts.net:4000/v1\n          apiKeyEnv: PROVIDERPROXY_API_KEY"
    },
    {
      "section": "~/.dsh/profiles/dsh-tui/cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "- insert:\n    - id: usage-limits\n      name: /path/to/dsh-usage-limits/tui.js\n      config: *usage\n```\n\n`name` must point at the entry file (`index.js` or `tui.js`), not the package directory. DSH finds the\nbrowser half through `package.json`. dsh-TUI 0.14.0 draws plugin status lines only in chat; the patch in\n`patches/` (applied by nix-config's `pkgs/dsh-tui.nix`) puts them on the Launchpad too. dsh web loads the\nplugin when `dsh-web` starts; `dst` loads it in each new process."
    },
    {
      "section": "Test",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm ci\nnpm test                                   # properties, host runtime, contracts, smoke\nDSH_TUI_DIR=<patched dsh-tui> npm run test:e2e:tui   # real dst in tmux\nnpm run test:e2e:web                       # real dsh web in Playwright"
    }
  ],
